.TH GLOW-KIT 1 "July 2026" "Fedora Glow Kit 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
glow-kit \- safely preview, apply, inspect, and revert Fedora Glow Kit
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B glow-kit
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B glow-kit
is the command-line interface for Fedora Glow Kit.
It keeps installation state in a private XDG state file, supports Fedora 44
KDE Plasma and GNOME Workstation, and does not collect telemetry.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Show target support and aggregate kit-managed state.
.TP
.B plan
Preview an ordered installation profile without changing the system.
.TP
.B apply
Run a confirmed installation flow.
.TP
.B revert
Remove changes recorded for one section or for the whole kit.
.TP
.B update
Preview safe update commands; add
.B --apply
to run them.
.TP
.B diagnostics
Print a local report without personal or device identifiers.
.TP
.B audit
Run the repository public-readiness checks.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates success.
One indicates cancellation or a failed maintenance command.
Two indicates invalid input, an unsupported target, or a refused export.
Installer exit codes may be propagated.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/fedora-plasma-glow-kit/install.state
Private record of changes made by the kit.
.TP
.I ~/.config/fedora-plasma-glow-kit/settings.json
Private GUI preferences.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR glow-kit-gui (1)
